ter, whose cut-off frequency is 8 kHz. The resultant process is sampled with a sampling interval of <em>T<sub>s</sub></em>. The minimum value of <em>T<sub>s</sub></em> (in μsec), for which the adjacent samples will be uncorrelated is ________.</p>\n<p>(Rounded off to one decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"62.5","high":"62.5"},"solution":"<p>62.5 (60.2 - 65.6)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/51018f13a336f3e19078b954f87dcda690cb1622.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B,C","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Assume the joint sample space <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> which has only three possible elements (1, 1), (2, 1) and (3, 3). The probabilities of these elements are to be</p>\n<p><em>P</em>(1, 1) = 0.3, <em>P</em>(2, 1) = 0.4 and <em>P</em>(3, 3) = 0.3 respectively. Then which of the following statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/90bfc051619a79734f444034774b314d2526a81f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/3e7c73e96f054dab6051c057361bd0cdcf9e4ff5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/880cfb9258625c843711ed001d35ce7a6f806cb0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/c94f01a1bdea4ba04b3d5e27544c940197b9f6b7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/9956c0838d222f14689350fc17760bd8c6df73c9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The entropy of noiseless discrete channel with ‘<em>n</em>’ input symbols <em>X</em> and ‘<em>m</em>’ output symbols <em>Y</em> is given by</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/361f4a59705492d2a63168c4